 assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 6cm fragment of breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x 5 8cm skin ellipse with a 3 5cm central  well healed  curvilinear scar and containing two sutures designated by the surgeon as  short superior  long lateral   The specimen is inked black superiorly and blue inferiorly and sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood filled biopsy cavity surrounded by a rubbery  ill defined  white fibrotic area which focally extends to the inked margin  superior   Also located in the lateral end of the specimen is a 0 5cm intraparenchymal lymph node  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity with superior margin  B H  Representative sections of biopsy cavity  I J  Representative tissue away from biopsy cavity  J contains intraparenchymal lymph node   Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Richard Graham Pingree  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Yes.
