Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty two year old female with three separate areas of malignant carcinoma in her left breast  a 1 2cm infiltrating ductal carcinoma in upper inner quadrant  and ductal carcinoma in situ in the lower inner quadrant and lateral portion of the breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SCATTERED FOCI  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITIES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN EIGHTEEN OF EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 59                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm attached skin ellipse  The skin ellipse contains a nipple  and is notable for a 3 0cm vertical scar  8 0cm lateral to the nipple  and a 3 5cm vertical scar  3 5cm medial to the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm diameter cavity  2 0cm deep to the medial scar  with a lobulated tan yellow  glistening wall  and a 0 1cm  yellow firm rim surrounding the defect  Also present is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm cavity  0 8cm deep to the lateral scar  with a smooth  tan pink lining  rimmed by 0 1cm of yellow  firm tissue  The medial cavity comes within 2 3cm of the medial superior resection margin  The lateral cavity comes within 1 5cm of the inferolateral resection margin  At one margin of the medial aspect is a stellate  soft  mottled yellow tan  il defined region about 2 5cm in greatest dimension  It extends to the margin of the specimen  Section Code  A E  medial cavity  representative sections  F  lateral cavity  closest approach to inked resection margin G J  lateral cavity  representative sections K  white  firm parenchymal streak  closest approach to inked resection margin L  white  firm parenchymal streak  representative section M  low axillary lymph nodes N O  distal axillary lymph nodes  R T  biopsy scar near medial margin U X  breast tissue Also received fresh  labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow  soft tissue fragment  bisected and submitted entirely in P  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Benjamin Alan Spencer  M D  PART A  MASTECTOMY  LEFT  PART B  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 39 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasive carcinoma is present lining the internal aspect of a previously opened cystic mass  Invasive carcinoma is also present in separate fragments of tissue submitted with the main specimen  The margins of resection cannot be accessed  Blood vessels and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The results of estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregularly shaped  yellow pink fibromembranous tissue forming the wall of a cystic cavity that was previously opened to reveal an irregular  trabeculated inner lining surface  The wall thickness ranges from REMOVED_DATE   1 0cm  The external surface of the wall is inked black  The internal surface is inked blue for orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue forming the wall of the cyst  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A D  Within the same specimen container are three irregularly shaped  pink yellow soft tissue fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Serially sectioning of these soft tissue fragments reveals no gross abnormalities  Representative sections of each fragment are submitted in cassette E  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew H Schulick  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
