d precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 31     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE INVASIVE TUMOR IS FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  NOTE  Although the close margin in slides E and F is not inked blue  it is at the junction of the green  anterior  and black  posterior  inks and opposite the yellow  inferior   and therefore is interpreted as superior  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tumor short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins  The specimen has a localization wire in place  The posterior margin is inked black  anterior green  inferior yellow  and superior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a metal clip surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm hemorrhagic focus  The fibrous tissue shows diffuse yellow orange foci and is focally dense with no discrete lesion  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as A F with the hemorrhagic focus as D F and the area designated by the clip and localization wire as F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node stitch at highest lymph node  is a 11 x 8 x 3 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch at one end designated as highest lymph node as per requisition  The specimen is divided into levels high  mid and low  Sectioning of the highest level reveals seven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the mid level reveals eleven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the lowest level reveals a single 1 9cm tan red lymph node  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  G  Highest lymph node bisected H  Five whole lymph nodes from the highest level I  One lymph nodes bisected from the highest level J  Five whole lymph nodes from the mid level K  One lymph node bisected from the mid level L  Three whole lymph nodes from mid level M  Two whole lymph nodes from mid level N  One whole lymph node bisected from the lowest level Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior lateral final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as O S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of unremarkable tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as T  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Sarah P Thayer  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST  INFERIOR LATERAL   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART C  BREAST  SUPERIOR   MARGIN PART D  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on excisional biopsy  comedo type                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PREDOMINATELY GRADE 1 WITH FOCAL GRADE 2  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND LOCATED FAR AWAY FROM MARGINS  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 15 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  3  ONE INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  4  COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The metastatic deposits in the lymph node aggregate to  0 1cm and consist of cohesive  whorled epithelial cell clusters located in the subcapsular sinuses  Their epithelial nature is confirmed by positive cytokeratin immunostaining  The slightly spindled morphology of the cells and the nuclear atypia are histologically similar to areas of the patient s ductal carcinoma in situ  Despite extensive examination and thorough sampling of the mastectomy specimen  no invasive carcinoma is found in the breast parenchyma itself  Review of the patient s prior biopsy specimens does not reveal any invasive component  Drs  Dennis Sgroi and Ben Pilch have reviewed selected slides and concur with the diagnosis of metastatic carcinoma  The ductal carcinoma in situ demonstrates a prominent spindle cell morphology in many areas  and there is also focal comedonecrosis  A Grimelius stain is negative for argyrophilic granules  Stains for ER  PR  and Her 2 neu will be attempted on the remaining lymph node tissue and will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 57                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block O   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  No tumor cells are seen in the section stained for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 26 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm tan pink nipple bearing skin ellipse and a 9 x 6 x 2cm axillary tail marked by a suture  On the tan pink skin surface there are two linear scars  one in the upper inner quadrant measuring 2 8cm in greatest dimension  and a second scar in the lower inner quadrant measuring 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two well healing biopsy cavities which are adjacent to each other  located in the medial aspect of the breast  The more medial of the cavities measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  The adjacent biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The cavities are surrounded by fat necrosis  The more medial of the cavities is 0 6cm to the closest posterior margin while the other cavity is 2cm to the closest posterior margin  The remainder of the breast is notable for diffuse thick fibrous tissue with numerous cysts ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 4cm  Additionally there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm pink papillary nodule in the midline of the breast which is located 2cm from t