Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  COMING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INFILTRATIVE COMPONENT  HEALING BIOPSY TRACT WITH FAT NECROSIS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood space invasion is identified Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  SKIN  LEFT SUPERIOR SUPERFICIAL   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  LEFT INFERIOR BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL NODE DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL  DEEP   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  DEEP   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  MICROCALCIFICATION  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 53 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 16     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   The lymph nodes do not show keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five specimens  Labeled  Left breast anterior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  1  now A  Labeled  Left breast lateral deep  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  2  now B  Labeled  Left breast superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  3  now C  Labeled  Left breast deep biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  4  now in D  Labeled  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a guide wire and sutures  The deep margin is inked black  the anterior surface is inked blue  and the medial surface is overinked red  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a 0 5cm irregularly shaped white fibrotic area near the anterior inked margin  Representative sections are submitted in E through N  Three specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  skin  superficial superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast tissue with an overlying  REMOVED_DATE x 1cm skin ellipse  The deep surface is inked black  Radial sectioning reveals no area suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Fully submitted in O  P  X and Y  Designated  skin  inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm skin ellipse with attached 0 4cm of pink tan tissue  The deep surface is inked black  The specimen is bivalved and fully submitted in Q and R  Designated  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of pink and yellow fibrofatty tissue  Multiple nodes are identified  and submitted in S W  Note that V and W each contain one fourth of the same node  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1    4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DX  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  SKIN  LEFT SUPERIOR SUPERFICIAL   EXCISIONAL BIOPS PART C  SKIN  LEFT INFERIOR BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR   BIOPSY PART F  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL  DEEP   BIOPSY PART G  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR   BIOPSY PART H  BREAST  LEFT  DEEP   BIOPSY   