achusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday August 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 36 51PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  91  to chromosome 17 signals  90  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday August 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 41 10PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Excision PART C  Breast  Right Medial  Margin   Excision PART D  Breast  Right Lateral  Margin   Excision PART E  Breast  Right Superior  Margin   Excision PART F  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 30 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II  100   DISPLAYING ENDOCRINE CHARACTERISTICS  POSSIBLY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  In situ carcinoma is not identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm fibrofatty tissue fragment  The tissue was inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white to gray mass abutting an inked margin  Representative sections were frozen as frozen section  1  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted  Section Code  A  closest margins  B E  representative sections of the mass  F  representative section of unremarkable breast  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA    INFILTRATING LOBULAR  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29 CLINICAL DATA  Breast carcinoma  Previous needle biopsy of right breast shows sclerosing carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   5 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SCHIRROUS TYPE  THE EXAMINED MARGINS ARE FREE OF TUMOR  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Most of the tumor is infiltrating  minor foci of intraductal carcinoma within the mass comprise less than 5 per cent  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  STROMAL FIBROSIS  CYSTS AND MILD FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 350 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast and axillary tissue with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  The skin ellipse contains a 5 5cm curvilinear non healed incision  Deep to the incision is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm biopsy cavity  lined with yellow fat and red hemorrhage  Sectioning of the breast reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm poorly demarcated  irregular  firm white mass adjacent to the biopsy cavity  The mass is close to the deep margin and close to the superior medial margin  extending from one to the other  It is 1 4cm deep to the skin at 1 0cm from the medial resection margin  A photograph is taken of the extension from superior medial to deep resection margin  Laterally the tumor infiltrates fat  Throughout the mass are focal hemorrhages  Within the superior medial aspect of tumor are multiple firm white nodules  ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm  The axillary tail contains multiple firm lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  AandB  skin with tumor and biopsy cavity C E  tumor with biopsy cavity and superior inked margin F I  tumor with deep resection margin J N  tumor with superomedial resection margin O  lateral tumor with infiltration fat P  medial most resection margin Q S  cross section of tumor  representative section T  representative section of lateral parenchyma  grossly uninvolved U  representative section of inferior parenchyma  grossly uninvolved V  representative section of superior parenchyma  grossly uninvolved W  representative of medial parenchyma  grossly uninvolved X Y  single lymph node Z AD  multiple lymph nodes each disected and entirely submitted  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY   report_end  , No.
