ient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm oriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue  which contains two localization wires  A short stitch designates the superior aspect  and a long stitch designates the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked as follow  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is thinly serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm  indurated  hemorrhagic area  consistent with the prior biopsy site  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  ill defined fibrous nodule  which appears to abut the anterior margin  and comes to within 2 4cm of the inferior margin  2 5cm of the posterior margin  and 2 7cm of the superior margin  The remaining parenchyma is approximately 60  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  and approximately 40  white fibrous tissue  Representative section is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previous biopsy site and surrounding area  with posterior margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and anterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm fibrous nodule  adjacent to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of fibrous tissue from area of localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections  submitted from medal to lateral  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla sentinel lymph node   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node  which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla  sentinel lymph node  2   is a