 the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 13                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  HOSPITAL MT AUBURN OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Linda Covell  M D  MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL DEPT OF PATH 330 MOUNT AUBURN STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  John Schuler  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  18 JUN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  6 Blocks  0   report_end  , No.
