ercent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 45     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm with axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The skin ellipse  with nipple  measures REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm  There is an ill defined hard nodule  tumor  1  inferior to the nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two other masses  One is located inferior and medial to the nipple  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm located 0 5cm from the inferior margin  tumor  2   The third   tumor  3  irregularly shaped white firm nodule is located deep to the second nodule  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  and is located 0 3cm from the closest inferior margin  Section Code  A B  first tumor inferior to the nipple  tumor to skin  C D  first tumor to normal breast  E  second tumor to closest margin  F H  second tumor to normal breast  I  third nodule  closest margin  J  third tumor to normal breast  In the axillary tail there are 19 tan rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are entirely submitted in cassettes K through N  Representative section of normal breast in cassette O  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Yes.
