 receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  are two pieces of fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm firm mass in the smaller specimen that abuts the inked resection margin  No frozen section is done on this lesion  The lesion is in submitted entirely in cassettes A through C  with representative sections of smaller biopsy in D and E  The larger biopsy is sectioned to reveal no grossly suspicious lesions  Representative sections of the larger biopsy are submitted in cassettes F through J  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY    report_end  , No.
