ositive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of firm white  poorly circumscribed mass surrounding the 0 4cm central duct  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in cassette A  Remainder submitted in B   G  from superficial to deep  distal end   The superficial end  short stitch  in B and the distal end  long stitch  in G  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST   INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Garth Rees Cosgrove  M D  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION  RIGHT    report_end  , No.
